From f006bc5dafeb0df3f397a17913ba97ab3ff1627e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:28:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 30/69] arm64: dts: qcom: Add Motorola Moto G 5G Plus (nairo)

Add the board devicetree: bootloader framebuffer, keys, reserved memory,
RPMh regulators for USB/UFS/SD, USB 2.0 peripheral mode, UFS, SD card,
the NT36672C touch controller on QUP1 SE1, and the PM7250B charger.

The phone's ABL selects DTBs by an exact "Qualcomm Technologies, Inc.
Lito" model string and aborts the boot when the stock dtbo overlay fails
to apply, so the model is set to that string and a generated "dtbo sink"
(sm7250-motorola-nairo-dtbo-sink.dtsi, from tools/gen_dtbo_sink.py)
resolves every label the stock overlays reference to inert nodes. Both are
workarounds for the stock bootloader and not suitable for upstream as is.

Hardware facts (addresses, GPIOs, regulator ranges, interrupts) were read
from the phone's live devicetree (/sys/firmware/fdt under LineageOS 23)
and the downstream sources. GPIOs 59-62 (fingerprint SPI) are owned by
TrustZone.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
